## the committed test after the fix
    ✓ with the 1 Hz meter interval running and wall-clock time passing during the outage: "Resynced" when the link is back, never "offline" again while ONLINE (1553 ms)
    ✓ the same outage without the wall-clock wait: "Resynced" (the case that always worked) (125 ms)
    ✓ "Resynced" hides after RESYNCED_BANNER_MS of real time; an outage while it shows turns it "offline" at once (3296 ms)
    ✓ the signal in a LOWER lane than the link change (the case that undid "Resynced"): "resynced", never "offline" after it (4 ms)
    ✓ the signal queued in a lower lane BEFORE the link change: "resynced" (1 ms)
    ✓ both in one lane, either order, and with an unrelated update pending elsewhere: "resynced" (5 ms)
    ✓ a resync never hides an outage: the signal while the link is still down keeps "offline" (2 ms)
